+## Incept
+
+1. **Name the seam and both ends before writing either.** Who produces, who consumes, how a
+   mismatch shows. The consuming end is what goes missing, because building the producer
+   feels like the work. *Someone will look* is not a reader.
+2. **Expand the shape first** — instances, polarities, quantities, kind; then where it lives
+   and who consumes it. Enumerate what is there, not what the shape implies. Where expansion
+   is expensive, say it was skipped.
+3. **Align before building.** `/align`, every incepted mechanism, no exceptions — and open it
+   by **explaining what the mechanism is** in plain terms. A mechanism nobody can describe is
+   one whose doc will describe the wrong thing. *(the operator, 2026-08-27)*
+4. **Assign the layer before the file exists**, or it gets decided by where the file landed.
+5. **Watch it fail.** Real defect, both polarities, at authoring time. A check never watched
+   failing is not a check, and it is believed harder than the note it replaced.
+6. **Run it over what already exists.** From landing it sees only new writes; every prior
+   violation is invisible to it forever. Fix what it finds, or **record the count** —
+   *nothing has tripped it since* means nothing while the backlog is unmeasured.
+7. **Produce the shape, not just the working part.** Steps 1–6 build a part and stop; that is
+   how two mechanisms were incepted in one day with no directory and no scripts. Not incepted
+   until it has: **a directory**, **a doc** carrying its moments table, **a register row**,
+   **whichever lifecycle pieces it actually needs**, and — if it accumulates — **a stated
+   contraction**. → *The mechanism directory*, *Moments*.
+
+   **Which lifecycle pieces, and each absence is declared rather than silent:**
+
+   | it has | when | when absent |
+   |---|---|---|
+   | `<slug>.rules.md` | it injects rules into instruction files it did not write | it injects none |
+   | `<slug>.install.js` / `.uninstall.js` | it has touchpoints that are **not** injected rules — a `settings.json` entry, a directory, a registration | injected rules are its only touchpoints; `inject-rules.js` is then the whole lifecycle |
+   | `<slug>.extract.js` | a clean copy takes some of its paths | a clean copy takes none — say which, and why, in the doc |
+   | `<slug>.announces.md` | its hooks place blocks in a session's context — the table declares each announcement's name, part module, event, **quiet condition** and the records it **watches**, and the part answers the runner through the `{name, body, message}` contract instead of writing stdout (definition: M00's doc; runner, ledger and staleness: M03's) | its hooks never speak, declared in the file as `none` so absence stays distinguishable from forgot |
+   | `<slug>.maintain.js` | its records have a checkable contract — then they are maintained by script, never by a session reading them. Check mode in the suite; fix mode on pickup; **format never content, live rows only**, archived history exempt *(0059, the operator, 2026-08-29)* | its records take judgment, or it has none |
+
+   **Some mechanisms are always on** and take none of the three: nothing can install or
+   uninstall the thing that defines what installing means. Say so in the register row.
+
+   - **Whether `install.js` earns its existence at all is still open** →
+     [0044.0220](../../../docs/tickets/0044.0220-mechanism-shape-lifecycle.md). A clean copy
+     copies files rather than running installers, so its only reader may be a person already
+     reading the doc. **Narrowed 2026-08-28**: two classes now legitimately have none, so the
+     question is no longer *does any mechanism need one* but *does the remaining class*.
+8. **Keep the instruction surface to instructions and compact examples.** Allowlist;
+   everything else goes to the sidecar.
+   - **A count is derived or it is not stated.** Point at the list; let the reader
+     count `[E11]`.
+
+     <!-- BEGIN INJECTED staggered-refiling -->
+     **Owned by `staggered-refiling`. Do not edit this block here** — it is written by `inject-rules.js` from that mechanism's rules file, and an edit made here is not kept — the next install overwrites it, printing what it took. Change it in [its doc](../../../mechanisms/staggered-refiling/staggered-refiling.doc.md).
+
+     **Log the occasion either way** — this rule is rule A of the staggered-refiling trial,
