+---
+name: reasoning
+description: >-
+  Use when a conclusion turns out to have been reached badly. Records the specimen and its
+  kind — `unexpanded-is` (never listed the cases), `unexpanded-lives` (never checked who reads
+  it), `proxy-trusted` (believed a summary instead of opening the thing), `property-substituted`
+  (measured one thing, claimed another), `jargon-not-glossary` (coined a word the glossary
+  already has), or `unclassified` — and changes nothing else. Invoke the moment it is noticed, and none of these is a reason not to: the conclusion
+  was already corrected, someone else caught it, nothing downstream broke, or it fits no kind
+  yet. The operator correcting your reasoning is always one, and is the strongest specimen
+  there is — it did not originate in your own judgment. Not for a thing the tree did wrong —
+  that is `/failure`. This asks what produced the conclusion; that asks what would have
+  caught it.
+---
+
+# Reasoning
+
+**Records. Nothing else.** No tier, no action, no mechanism earned, no disposition. A specimen
+and a kind, appended to `memory/reasoning.md`.
+
+The restraint is deliberate: [0028](../../../docs/tickets/0028-reasoning-failure-class.md) is
+**deferred by the operator** until they have read some reasoning literature, on the grounds
+that a taxonomy should not be settled with the instruments at hand. Capture does not wait on
+that; classification does.
+
+## The line against `/failure`
+
+| | asks | register |
+|---|---|---|
+| **`/failure`** | what would have caught it — detection | `memory/failures.md` |
+| **`/reasoning`** | what produced the conclusion — generation | `memory/reasoning.md` |
+
+**One event can be both**, and then it gets two entries with different content, not one entry
+in two places. The wrong conclusion is the specimen; whatever the tree failed to catch is the
+failure.
+
+**`memory/failures.md` cannot hold these.** Its axes are `caught by` and `tier`, and both ask
+about delivery — so every reasoning specimen lands at *tier 1, no memory of it anywhere*.
+True, and the same verdict for defects with entirely different fixes.
+
+## Recording one
+
+Append to `memory/reasoning.md`:
+
+```
+### <date> — <one line: the conclusion, not the correction>
+- **kind:** <slug, or `unclassified`>
+- **what I concluded:**
+- **what was true:**
+- **the cheap step not taken:** what would have shown it, at what cost
+- **caught by:** self | operator, asserted | operator, question | testing | another party | nothing until after
+```
+
+**`operator, asserted` and `operator, question` are different events and the second is the
+one that indicts.** Asserted means they knew I was wrong and said so — it needed knowledge I
+did not have. **Question means they asked something neutral and answerable, and the answer
+exposed it** — *what does a stall actually mean*, *where did the doc go*, *why has no
+mechanism got scripts*. Those were available to me. The question **is** the cheap expansion
+0028 says was one step away, asked by somebody else.
+
+Quote the question. A specimen whose origin is a question carries the sentence that produced
+it, because the sentence is the mechanism that would have worked.
+
+**Name the conclusion, not the fix.** *Pointed a behaviour gap at a migration ticket* is a
+specimen; *fixed the ticket references* is not.
+
+**`unclassified` is a first-class answer** and the most useful row in a draft vocabulary — a
+kind invented to receive an awkward specimen is the defect this whole mechanism exists to
+catch, performed on itself.
+
+**Record `unclassified`, then `/align` — never invent the kind here.** A vocabulary is a
+shape, and adding to one from inside the session that hit the awkward case is the same act
+0028 refuses: the specimen gets bent toward whatever was reachable, and the bending is
+invisible afterwards. `/align` is the only path a kind is added by, and it may equally
+conclude the specimen belongs to an existing kind, or that two kinds should merge.
+
+**A run of `unclassified` rows is the signal, not an embarrassment.** It is what tells 0028's
+alignment where the draft is thin, and a file with none of them is more likely being forced
+than being right.
+
+## The draft kinds
+
+**Draft, open, and not the agent's to settle** (0028). Four so far, and the first two are
+that ticket's named shape — *a shape conceived and acted on without being expanded, when
+expanding was cheap*, on its two axes.
+
+| kind | the expansion not taken |
+|---|---|
+| `unexpanded-is` | the thing's own instances, polarities, quantities, kind |
+| `unexpanded-lives` | its consumers, moments, routes — where it sits |
+| `proxy-trusted` | asserted from a description of the thing rather than the thing |
+| `property-substituted` | one property read as another — completeness as correctness |
+| `jargon-not-glossary` | a term coined where `core/glossary.md` already governs one |
+
+The middle two **resist** 0028's shape rather than extending it: nothing was un-expanded, the
+wrong question was asked. Recorded that way rather than forced into the existing name.
+
+**Open `core/glossary.md` before using a term of art.** A coinage cannot be checked — a
+glossary governs only the words it knows — which is what `jargon-not-glossary` records.
+*(the operator, 2026-08-29)*
+
+**The description names the kinds; this table says what they mean.** One home each, and a
+session carrying only tier 1 knows the vocabulary without invoking anything.
+*(the operator, 2026-08-29)* → [EVIDENCE.md](./EVIDENCE.md)
+
+## What this does not do
+
+- **No disposition.** Nothing here is triaged, closed or graded. `/audit` reads across
+  sessions; a single session may not conclude from its own specimens (meta-rule 6).
+- **No mechanism.** A specimen never earns a rule here. That is 0028's, after the reading.
+- **No retrofit.** Reclassifying historical `memory/failures.md` entries against a vocabulary
+  invented this week would bake the draft in → [0053](../../../docs/tickets/0053-reasoning-specimens-retrofit.md).

