--- L2/ticket/SKILL.md
+++ L/ticket/SKILL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@
+---
+name: ticket
+description: >-
+  Decompose work into independently-completable tickets and register them on the queue in
+  the same pass. Use to mint a ticket — possibly a single one — for anything that will
+  outlive the session that noticed it; to grade a built one against its artifacts, when
+  this session built none of it; and to close one whose criteria have been graded.
+---
+
+# Decompose into tickets
+
+Break work into independently-grabbable slices, written as markdown under
+`docs/tickets/`. The parent is a concern at inception, a coarse ticket when zooming in,
+or the chunk under discussion; the same slicing applies at every resolution.
+
+The shape of a ticket, its naming, and the queue are
+[TICKET-FORMAT.md](./TICKET-FORMAT.md)'s. Read it before writing one; restate none of it.
+
+## A ticket struck again records the strike
+
+Where the work you are doing shows an existing ticket costing something again — a defect it
+would have prevented, a decision it is blocking — log one line before anything else:
+
+```bash
+node .agents/lib/strike.js <ticket-slug> "one line"
+```
+
+It increments `- **Strikes:** N` on the ticket. `/triage` ranks by *what recurrence would
+cost*; without this that term is estimated by the session doing the ranking, and with it, it
+is counted. Slug, never number. Read at wake by `queue-next.js`.
+→ [EVIDENCE.md](./EVIDENCE.md)
+
+## Why a ticket rather than a note
+
+A concern records that something is unresolved. A ticket carries what would resolve it —
+the criteria, the dependency, and the bar for closing. An open question with no ticket
+is a question nobody has decided how to answer, which is the state most of them stay in.
+
+Mint one for anything that will outlive the session. A session that ends is a session
+whose intentions evaporate.
+
+## Process
+
+### 1. Locate the parent
+
+Ask for the parent's path unless it is clear from context. Read it if it is not already
+in context. When the parent is the chunk under discussion there is no file — the ticket
+must then carry its own context.
+
+### 2. Draft slices
+
+Each slice is independently completable and verifiable on its own. Prefer many thin
+slices over few thick ones. A chunk already ticket-sized yields a single ticket — a
+valid outcome, not a failed decomposition.
+
+Mark each **AFK** or **HITL** honestly. This repo runs unattended daily, so the mark is
+the autonomy boundary rather than a note about convenience: AFK means the cron may close
+it alone. A slice whose closing needs a judgment the evidence cannot supply is HITL, and
+saying so is the whole value of the field.
+
+A slice blocked on an unresolved decision begins as a **decision-bearing HITL ticket**.
+It is the eventual work in an earlier phase, not a separate decision slice; name it for
+the outcome it will deliver.
+
+### 3. Quiz
+
+Present the breakdown as a numbered list — title, type, depends on, what of the parent it
+covers. Ask whether the granularity and dependencies are right, whether anything should
+merge or split, and whether the AFK/HITL marks are honest. Iterate until approved.
+
+**Quiz only what is genuinely forked.** Where the decomposition is uncontroversial, register
+it and report rather than asking — attended or not. Someone being available to answer is not
+a reason to spend their attention, and having a recommendation you expect to be taken is the
+tell that there was no fork. Never flip a HITL mark to clear a stall.
+
+### 4. Write and register
+
+Create in dependency order so `Depends on` can reference real filenames. A completed
+blocker lives in `done/` — reference it there. Update the queue in the same pass; a
+ticket that exists only as a file is not on the queue.
+
+### 5. Grading
+
+The act, its bar, and the field it writes are [TICKET-FORMAT.md](./TICKET-FORMAT.md)'s
+*Grading — the act*; this step restates none of it. The moment is a session holding a
+built ticket it did not build — read each criterion against the artifact, not the ticket's
+account of it. `grading-due.js` names what is owed, at `/conclude`.
+
+### 6. Completing
+
+When every box is checked, close through `node .agents/scripts/close-ticket.js <slug>`
+(`--dry` first) — it moves the file to `docs/tickets/done/`, repairs the citations that
+pointed at it, and leaves frozen records dangling by design. Never by hand: the by-hand
+road is how a 2026-08-26 session priced nine reference repairs as too expensive and argued
+for leaving a finished ticket in the queue. Do not close or modify the parent — a parent
+completes on its own criteria, never by its children emptying out.
+
+## Altitude
+
+A slice whose criteria cannot be written as observable outcomes is not yet a ticket →
+`/align` first. Prefer a criterion that a check can verify over one a reader must
+remember to verify.
+
+<project-local>
+Concern promotion: **the row leaves `docs/concerns.md` entirely**, as a ticketed failure
+leaves its register *(the operator, 2026-08-30)*. Move the deliberation into the ticket and
+say there which `C<n>` it came from — ids are never reused, so the citation resolves whether
+or not a row still carries it. A concern and a ticket must never hold two copies of the same
+argument.
+</project-local>

### ticket/TICKET-FORMAT.md [missing]
--- L2/ticket/TICKET-FORMAT.md
+++ L/ticket/TICKET-FORMAT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,264 @@
+# Ticket format
+
+Project-local, divergent by design. Where a ticket sits in the document family is
+[the loop](../../../core/process.md)'s. This shelf holds what `/ticket` owns: the
+naming scheme, the delivery-state vocabulary, and the shape of the ticket and the queue.
+
+This repo has no releases, so positions carry no release prefix. It has an unattended
+daily cron, which makes `Type` load-bearing rather than advisory.
+
+## Numbering
+
+```
+docs/tickets/done/0040-regrade-horizon-table.md
+                   │    └── slug — what the ticket is. Never changes. Cite by this.
+                   └─────── position — global. Changes when priority changes.
+```
+
+- Positions step by 10. Insert by splitting the difference: `0045`, then `0042`. Four
+  digits always — longer breaks numeric ordering. When a gap is exhausted, take the
+  nearest free slot on the correct side and note the placement in the queue row.
+- Allocate where the ticket will actually be worked, checking `docs/tickets/` and
+  `docs/tickets/done/` for the surrounding positions.
+- A subticket appends a level: `0040.0010`. It means "is a child of", nothing else —
+  work merely filed after `0040` takes `0045`.
+- Completed tickets keep their number.
+- **Cite by slug, never by number.** Positions move when priority moves; slugs do not.
+
+## Status
+
+`Done` · `In progress` · `Ready` · `Partial` · `Planned` · `Blocked` · `Declined` · `Folded`
+
+- **Ready** — dependencies complete, work can start. **Planned** — they are not.
+- **Partial** — some of it landed; criteria remain open.
+- **Blocked** — stuck for a reason *other than* an incomplete dependency. Waiting on a
+  dependency is `Planned`, never `Blocked`.
+- **Declined** — we are not doing this, and here is what not doing it costs. The **only**
+  status that leaves the queue with boxes unchecked, and it carries a `## Why declined`
+  section stating the price. Added 2026-08-29 ([0054](../../../docs/tickets/done/0054-a-queue-pass-leaves-a-record.md)):
+  `/triage` has listed *Declined* as a disposition since it was written and the tree had no
+  way to execute one — no status meant refused, `done/` was the only directory, and the mover
+  refuses unchecked boxes, which a declined ticket has by definition. So a pass reaching that
+  conclusion had to leave the row looking exactly like work that was still wanted.
+- One parenthetical qualifier allowed: `Planned (needs the operator)`, `Done (split)`.
+  `Done` carries its date, and so does `Declined`.
+
+### Declining, concretely
+
+`- **Status:** Declined (YYYY-MM-DD)` plus a `## Why declined` section, then
+`node .agents/scripts/close-ticket.js <slug> --decline`, which moves it to
+`docs/tickets/declined/` and repairs every citation. **The price is enforced, not requested**:
+the mover refuses a ticket whose status is not `Declined` or whose `## Why declined` is
+missing or empty. `/triage`'s *a decline with no price is a deferral wearing better clothes*
+has been a rule since that skill was written, and this is the first thing that checks it.
+
+**A decline is not a failure and is not a deletion.** The file keeps its evidence, its
+strikes and its history; what changes is that the queue stops offering it as work. Reversing
+one is `git mv` back and a status edit — the same cost as any other row move.
+
+### Folding, concretely
+
+**Folded** — the work moved into another ticket that will do it. The third road out, and the
+second that leaves with boxes unchecked. `- **Status:** Folded (YYYY-MM-DD)` plus
+`node .agents/scripts/close-ticket.js <slug> --fold-into=<target>`, which moves it to
+`docs/tickets/done/` and repairs every citation.
+
+**The target must be open and must name the folded slug**, and the mover refuses otherwise.
+That is folding's equivalent of the price a decline carries: a fold whose destination does not
+know about it is a deletion pretending. Record in the target what it absorbed and which
+criteria came with it.
+
+**`--fold-into=<slug>`, never a detached value** — the ticket to move is the first argument not
+starting with `--`, so a detached target would be read as the ticket.
+
+**Only a fully folded ticket leaves.** Where some criteria move and others stay, the ticket
+stays open with the moved ones struck through — that is `Partial`, and it needs nothing new.
+
+**Declined and Folded are not interchangeable.** Declined is *this will not happen, and here is
+the price*; folded work is happening, elsewhere. A reader searching `declined/` must not find
+absorbed work.
+
+### Serving an experiment
+
+**An experiment is not a ticket status and does not live in a ticket.** It has its own
+entity in [`experiments/`](../../../experiments/README.md), which is what its
+rules, scripts, memory files, tickets and readings link to. A ticket may **devise** one,
+**build** part of one, or **own a decision** it reaches — three different jobs, and a
+ticket doing any of them carries the link:
+
+```
+- **Experiment:** [handle-beside-ref](../experiments/handle-beside-ref.md)
+```
+
+Placed with `Depends on`. The ticket keeps its own `Status`, which tracks *its* delivery
+and never the experiment's — a fully-built mechanism can be under experiment, so `Done`
+on the ticket and a running experiment are consistent and common.
+
+**Build it properly anyway.** A flimsy mechanism under test yields readings about the
+flimsiness. Robustness is what makes the reading about the hypothesis.
+
+## Type — what the cron may touch
+
+- **AFK** — the unattended daily run may complete this alone.
+- **HITL** — needs the operator. A cron run may prepare it, never close it.
+
+A ticket is HITL when closing it would require a judgment the evidence cannot supply:
+a decision only the operator can make, or a claim about them. Prefer AFK where honest;
+do not launder a judgment into AFK because the cron would otherwise stall.
+
+## Retyping — the act
+
+**A ticket goes `HITL → AFK` when the decision it was `HITL` for has been made, and the mark of
+that is a dated operator ruling on the ticket:**
+
+```
+## Resolved — the operator, YYYY-MM-DD
+```
+
+(or `## Resolutions — … the operator … YYYY-MM-DD`). The operator decides in conversation and
+writes nothing; the session records the ruling under that heading, verbatim where it can be,
+then changes `Type:`. Both may land in one edit. `guard-ticket-type.js` reads the file's
+after-state for the heading and refuses the retype without it — strict rule 4, which forbids
+the retype *to clear a stall*, and a stall is exactly a row with no ruling on it.
+
+**The mark is the operator's word and may not be invented.** A session that writes a
+*the operator, date* line the operator did not say has forged a ruling, which is a worse act
+than the retype and leaves a dated lie in history. *(Amended 2026-09-03 → `docs/rules-evidence.md`,
+Rule 4; the moment belongs to `/align`.)*
+
+## Grading — the act
+
+Someone who built none of it reads each criterion against the artifact and says whether it
+holds. A later session qualifies; so does a person. `.agents/scripts/grading-due.js` names the
+rows owed a grader and withholds the running session's own.
+
+**Per criterion, three moves and no fourth.** Tick it. Leave it. Or strike it through and write
+what is true instead — a criterion whose premise has moved is answered by restating it, never
+by ticking it loosely and never by deleting it.
+
+**Read the artifact, not the ticket's account of it.** A criterion claiming a check was watched
+failing is graded by breaking the thing and watching it. Graded any other way, it is graded on
+the builder's word, which is the reading meta-rule 6 refuses.
+
+**Running the commands is not the grading.** Execution is reproducible and carries no author,
+so a grader repeating it learns nothing the builder did not already have. What cannot be
+laundered is the judgment: are these the right criteria, and does the artifact meet them.
+
+**Ask the question the criteria do not contain — did this deliver its `Outcome`.** A builder
+writes criteria it can meet, so a ticket with every box ticked may still be `Partial`, and that
+verdict is available only to someone who did not write the boxes.
+
+**Close the pass by writing the field, whatever the verdict:**
+
+```
+- **Grading:** graded by {session NNNN | name}, YYYY-MM-DD — {n} of {m}. {What is not met.}
+```
+
+Every box ticked → `node .agents/scripts/close-ticket.js <slug>`. Otherwise the row stays,
+graded, with the field naming what it waits on. **Grading is not closing**, and a pass that
+grades and closes nothing is complete.
+
+## Touches — the grading bar
+
+A ticket that would move a graded statement names the layer it touches and what would
+license the move. This is the bar for closing it, visible before the work starts.
+
+| Layer touched | Closing requires |
+|---|---|
+| `[bone]` | A contradicting measurement. Name where it would come from. |
+| `[muscle]` | One clear counter-example. |
+| `[skin]` | Nothing beyond doing the work. |
+| unlabelled | Nothing — but say so, so the absence is deliberate. |
+
+Layers and their evidence are `memory/skills.md`'s. Never restate them here.
+
+## The ticket
+
+```md
+# {Title}
+
+- **Status:** {value} {(qualifier)}
+- **Mechanism:** {slug or M-number}{, second}
+- **Type:** HITL | AFK
+- **Strikes:** {n} — last {YYYY-MM-DD}: {what struck it}
+- **Grading:** awaiting — built by session NNNN | graded by session NNNN, YYYY-MM-DD
+- **Touches:** [{layer}] {statement} — {what would license the move}
+- **Depends on:** [{title}](./NNNN-slug.md) ({what it supplies})
+- **Blocks:** [{title}](./NNNN-slug.md) — {why}
+- **Outcome:** {the delivered change, one or two sentences}
+
+## Parent
+## {Why this exists}          ← 0..n, titled for the claim each argues
+## What to build
+## Decisions this ticket owns
+## Acceptance criteria
+## Out of scope
+```
+
+Always present: `Status`, `Type`, `Outcome`, `What to build`, `Acceptance criteria`.
+The rest appear when they have something to say. Header order as above; `Outcome` last.
+
+| Section | Rule |
+|---|---|
+| `Strikes` | **Never written by hand.** `node .agents/lib/strike.js <slug> "<one line>"` increments it at the moment something goes wrong that this ticket bears on. Absent means never struck. Read at wake by `queue-next.js`. It is the term `/triage` already ranks by — *what recurrence would cost* — counted rather than estimated by the session doing the ranking. **The count is not the account:** `CLAUDE.md` meta-rule 1 decides whether an *entry* is worth carrying and often says no; all three of its outcomes still record the one line. **Outside evidence strikes too** — a point conceded to a citizen or verified against this tree, its note carrying `cN` and the handle. The bar is our own response and never their reliability → `/comment`, *A concession is a strike*. |
+| `Mechanism` | Which mechanism this ticket is about, by slug or `M`-number, several comma-separated. Present whenever it is about one; absent means it is about none, which is a claim and not a shrug. **`/maintain`'s survey pulls tickets by this field**, so a ticket naming none is invisible to the next maintenance of the thing it changes. The register's `tickets` cell is the other half and is transcribed by hand: on 2026-08-30 it named neither `0066` on M24 nor `0031` on M06, each written for that mechanism the day before → [0048](../../../docs/tickets/0048-records-name-their-mechanism.md). |
+| `Grading` | Written by `/conclude` when work lands, never by the session claiming its own criteria. Read by `.agents/scripts/grading-due.js`, which withholds rows the running session built. Absent on a ticket nothing has landed against; **absent on one that has ticks is a defect the enumeration reports.** |
+| `Title` | Names the outcome, not the mechanism. No number. |
+| `Parent` | The durable doc owning the context — a concern, a skill, a graded statement. Never a session. |
+| Narrative | Titled for what it argues. Link the evidence; cite the board post or the measurement. Omit when the framing is uncontested. |
+| `What to build` | End-to-end behavior. Each constraint carries its reason. |
+| `Decisions this ticket owns` | One bullet per open question, each saying why it cannot be answered yet. |
+| `Acceptance criteria` | Checkboxes, each observably true when done. |
+| `Out of scope` | What a reader expects and will not find, each with its actual home. |
+| `Outcome` | Observable change, never file shape. Copied verbatim into the queue. |
+
+### Acceptance criteria
+
+- **Prefer a check to a criterion.** If a box could be a hook instead of a sentence
+  someone must verify, write the hook and say so. A criterion a reader must remember to
+  check is the weaker instrument (`memory/skills.md`, bone).
+- Name the instrument when a naive check would pass for the wrong reason.
+- Never write a criterion asserting completeness. That claim decays as it is made.
+- Check a box only for work that satisfied it; one satisfied early is checked with a date.
+
+### Conventions
+
+- Cite by slug through a relative link; add the `done/` segment when the target completes.
+  `.agents/scripts/close-ticket.js <slug>` performs the move and every repair — it refuses a
+  ticket with an unchecked box, and rewrites only strings carrying a path, so a sealed
+  expectation token in `memory/continuity/` that looks like a slug is left alone. It also
+  **skips every path `frozen-paths.js` names and reports which**, so a citation inside a
+  session record or an archive keeps pointing where it pointed when it was written; those
+  dangle by design and `links-resolve.js` counts them as frozen-and-expected. **So a grep for
+  the old path after a close is not expected to come back empty** — it comes back with exactly
+  the frozen hits the mover listed. The queue row and `Status` stay yours.
+- Reference `docs/concerns.md`, `memory/skills.md`, and board threads; never restate them.
+- Strike superseded text, answer inline in bold, keep the question. **A ticked criterion
+  naming a path nothing in the tree answers is reported** by
+  `.agents/scripts/criteria-paths.js`, asserted in the suite against a standing mark — so a
+  bar that decayed into fiction is caught rather than found by a grader going to run it. Put
+  the names of vanished artifacts in the grading section, not inside the criterion: the check
+  cannot tell *this path is gone* from *this path is required*.
+- Date anything that changed after minting.
+- Update the queue in the same pass.
+
+## The queue
+
+`docs/tickets/README.md`.
+
+```md
+# Delivery status
+**Last updated:** YYYY-MM-DD
+**Current stage:** {what landed, what is next, links to both}
+
+## Delivery map
+## Decisions still owned by tickets
+## Cron boundary
+```
+
+| Section | Rule |
+|---|---|
